    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47707" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θαιρός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pivot of a door</i> or
			<i>gate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῆξε δ᾽ ἀπ᾽ ἀμφοτέρους θαιρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.459
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				3.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				1.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>axle</i> of a chariot, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				596
			</span></i>. (Perh. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θϝᾰρ</span>-<i>yos</i>,
			cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύρα</span>.)</div>
